 - Avoiding recursion-depth limits: Python's default recursion limit (about 1000) can be exceeded by recursive DFS or divide-and-conquer on large inputs. Prefer iterative solutions (explicit stacks, queues, or iterative BFS/DFS) where recursion depth could grow with the input size. If recursion is unavoidable, use `sys.setrecursionlimit(...)` together with `threading.stack_size(...)` and run the solver in a thread with a large stack.
 """
